// # qa - Anchor for Agents
//
// Logline: Hostile probes and double-run determinism tests for the ooda-tui harness.
//
// Setup: Pure structural file. Each .oo probe is a fail-closed test. Double-run: Run_1 == Run_2 per rules.oot 1.10.
//
// Beats:
//   1. argv.oo - parse all 10 flags, error cases, env contract.
//   2. probe_slash.oo - invoke each of 17 slash commands, verify effects.
//   3. theme_probe.oo - render every token, snapshot match against expected ANSI.
//   4. mcp_handshake.oo - spawn ooda-mcp, list tools.
//   5. lsp_init.oo - spawn ooda-lsp, initialize, receive diagnostics.
//   6. llm_mock.oo - provider client with mocked HTTP.
//   7. multi_provider.oo - connect N providers, health check.
//   8. probe_teamwork.oo - spawn 4 mock agents, dashboard updates, proofs aggregate.
//   9. smoke.oo - end-to-end TUI launch, login, ask, exit.
//   10. probe_preset.oo - workflow presets (kernel, frontend, audit, zen) and fail-closed flags.
//   11. probe_sanitize.oo - shell metacharacters injection negative falsification.
//   12. probe_slash_dynamic.oo - dynamic external slash script fallback in plugins dir.
//   13. probe_temp_perm.oo - temporary file mode 0600 validation on credential headers.
//   14. e2e_tier1_f1_f3.oo - Tier 1 coverage for Features 1-3.
//   15. e2e_tier1_f4_f6.oo - Tier 1 coverage for Features 4-6.
//   16. e2e_tier1_f7_f9.oo - Tier 1 coverage for Features 7-9.
//   17. e2e_tier1_f10_f12.oo - Tier 1 coverage for Features 10-12.
//   18. e2e_tier2_b1_b3.oo - Tier 2 boundary analysis for Boundaries 1-3.
//   19. e2e_tier2_b4_b6.oo - Tier 2 boundary analysis for Boundaries 4-6.
//   20. e2e_tier2_b7_b9.oo - Tier 2 boundary analysis for Boundaries 7-9.
//   21. e2e_tier2_b10_b12.oo - Tier 2 boundary analysis for Boundaries 10-12.
//   22. e2e_tier3_pairwise.oo - Tier 3 pairwise cross-feature combinations.
//   23. e2e_tier4_scenarios.oo - Tier 4 real-world application scenarios.
//   24. e2e_master.oo - Master runner executing full 138-test E2E suite.

// residual: probes are spawned as separate ooda-tui builds via CI. They share no source with the main binary.
